BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Moonlit Mystic Graveyard Ghost Tours
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260304
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261130
DTSTAMP:20260917T152608Z
UID:87cc9db5307d7b0277c324c812fb@ctvisit-calendar
DESCRIPTION:There’s nothing more intimately haunting than a colonial bur
 ial ground and Mystic boasts some of the most fascinating and haunted buri
 al grounds around. The Graveyard Ghost tour takes place at Whitehall Buria
 l Ground just off Hendel Drive in Mystic. Whitehall Burial Ground establis
 hed in the 1660’s was one of the common burial places of Mystic until th
 e rural landscape movement arrived to Mystic in 1854. Our Graveyard Ghost 
 Tour tells tales of some of Mystic’s most famous residents.\n\nSource: h
 ttps://ctvisit.com/events/moonlit-mystic-graveyard-ghost-tours-1
LOCATION:Hendel Drive\, Mystic CT\, 06355
URL:https://ctvisit.com/events/moonlit-mystic-graveyard-ghost-tours-1
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Independence Revisited: Sharon in 1776\, 1876 & 1976
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260422
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270116
DTSTAMP:20260917T152608Z
UID:23ea6076988d4b14f8723179c35d@ctvisit-calendar
DESCRIPTION:By examining Sharon through the lens of three pivotal mileston
 es—1776\, 1876\, and 1976—the exhibition explores how broader national
  transformations informed the local experience. Independence Revisited beg
 ins with a study of 18th-century life and follows the town’s physical\, 
 social\, and political trajectory\, ultimately investigating how Sharon ch
 ose to commemorate\, interpret\, or overlook its revolutionary heritage du
 ring these defining moments in American history.\n\nSource: https://ctvisi
 t.com/events/independence-revisited-sharon-1776-1876-1976
LOCATION:Sharon Historical Society & Museum\, 18 Main Street\, Sharon CT\,
  06069
URL:https://ctvisit.com/events/independence-revisited-sharon-1776-1876-197
 6
END:VEVENT
